f(9,'prompt','In a simplified COW model, 10,000 writes each touch a different shared COW unit. Compare 4 KiB units with 2 MiB units, assuming every fault copies the full unit and no split/reuse path. What additional backing is copied? This is arithmetic, not a prediction of current Redis/Linux behavior.','ModernTHPnotalwayswholecopy norwidelyscatteredguaranteeuniquehugepages.',th)
f(9,'workedExample','Under the explicit full-unit-copy model, 10,000 × 4 KiB = 40,000 KiB = 39.0625 MiB. For 2 MiB units, 10,000 × 2 MiB = 20,000 MiB = 19.53125 GiB. Linux may split mappings or reuse exclusive backing, so these numbers do not follow merely from THP=always. Redis documents potential THP costs; actual amplification must be measured.','Retaincorrectarithmeticwithmodelscope.',th)
