f(11,'explanation','False. zram is primarily a compressed RAM block device; optional configured writeback can use a backing device. zswap is a separate compressed cache in front of swap.','Zramdiskoptional.',zr,o=4)
f(11,'workedExample','Preserving arbitrary live anonymous data during reclaim normally requires swap backing, while freed/discardable pages can be released without it. Swap entries can resolve through resident swap cache, zswap or the device, so not every swap-related fault reads disk. vm.swappiness is a reclaim-cost preference, not an off switch. zram stores compressed data in RAM and can optionally use configured writeback.','Multiplefalseuniversals.',ma+zs+zr)
